gth:**\n- My cards: 10♥, 8♠\n- Board: 3♥, 9♥, 10♦\n- I have a pair of 10s (middle pair)\n\n**Potential Draws:**\n- I have a backdoor flush draw in hearts (10♥ and 3♥, 9♥ on board - need 2 more hearts)\n- Potential straight draw: I have 10-8, board has 9. If a 7 and J come, I could make a straight, but this requires both turn and river to be specific cards (very unlikely)\n\n**Opponent Analysis:**\n- Opponent has only called/checked so far (passive play)\n- This could indicate: weak hand, slow-playing a strong hand, or drawing hand\n- With this board (3-9-10 rainbow), opponent likely doesn't have a strong made hand yet or they would have bet\n\n**Position & Pot Control:**\n- Opponent checked on the flop, now it's my turn\n- Current pot is small (just blinds and calls)\n- I'm slightly ahead in chips (19,900 vs 20,000)\n\n**Hand Evaluation:**\nA pair of 10s on this board is reasonably strong but vulnerable:\n- **Pros**: Middle pair, top kicker (considering my 10)\n- **Cons**: \n  - Any overpair (JJ, QQ, KK, AA) beats me\n  - Opponent could have 9-10, A-10, K-10 for better two pair or better kicker\n  - Two more cards to come (turn and river) give opponent many opportunities to improve\n\n**Strategic Options:**\n1. **Check (0)**: Safe, pot control, see turn for free. Risk: opponent might have drawing hand that improves\n2. **Raise (100+)**: Build pot with decent hand, gather information, potentially fold out weaker hands or draws\n3. **Fold (-1)**: Too conservative with middle pair\n4. **All-in (-2)**: Way too aggressive for middle pair with 2 cards to come\n\nReason:\n\nI should make a modest raise of around 100-200 chips. This accomplishes several goals:\n1. **Value betting**: My pair of 10s is likely ahead given opponent's passive play\n2. **Information gathering**: Opponent's response will tell me a lot about their hand strength\n3. **Protection**: Charges draws and prevents free cards that could beat me\n4. **Pot building**: If I have the best hand, I want to build