ry aggressive, might scare away calling hands\n\nReason: \nI have three Kings, which is a very strong hand. My opponent has been passively calling throughout, suggesting they have a decent but not premium hand. Given the board texture and their calling pattern, they likely have a pair or possibly two pair. Betting around 1,200-1,500 chips (about half pot to pot-sized bet) will extract value from hands they've shown willingness to call with, while not being so large that it scares away all worse hands. This sizing maintains the story of my betting pattern while maximizing expected value.\n\nAnswer: 1200"}
